==Strategy==
Seeing as half the enemies in the stage are Floating, units like [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] and [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] will do you well in this stage. Bring [[Long Distance]] units as well. Other than that, the main goal is to survive the 2 Gobbles. If you can do that, then the Li'l Bun Buns and Mooths will pose no issue, as they can't push on their own. To accomplish this, you can try chipping them from behind THE FOLIVOREAN with Long Distance units like [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] or [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] hits, but the more consistent strategy is to abuse THE FOLIVOREAN's long attack rate to sneak in hits from [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]].

As the Mooths and Gobbles have shorter standing range, when THE FOLIVOREAN attacks, the former 2 get an opportunity to push forward during the latter's attack downtime, exposing them to damage like Bullet Train Cat, Fishman Cat, but most importantly Can Can Cat. If you can accomplish this twice on both Gobbles, the stage is won.

